    "result_text": "Done. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## What I changed\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by its starting calendar year):\n\n1. **`mapper/Fiscal.java`** (new, small cohesive helper) \u2014 `startYear(LocalDate)` returns the calendar year the containing fiscal year began in (Jul\u2013Dec \u2192 same year, Jan\u2013Jun \u2192 previous year); `label(LocalDate)` formats it as `FY<YY>`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 three minimal, one-line-ish edits, each keeping the touched method simple:\n   - `membershipNumber`: `-M<YY>` now uses the fiscal start year instead of the calendar year.\n   - `membershipTenured`: tenure is now \"at least one fiscal year has elapsed\" (`Fiscal.startYear(reg) < Fiscal.startYear(now)`) instead of a 365-day window.\n   - Added a `fiscalYear` mapping expression on `toOwnerDto` producing `FY<YY>` from the (business-day-adjusted) registration date.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it, and refreshed the `membershipNumber` description.\n\n## Structural impact\n\nKept low deliberately: the fiscal logic lives in one tiny new class with no surrounding complexity, so the `OwnerMapper` methods stay simple delegations (no growth in their cyclomatic complexity) rather than absorbing branching logic that would have paid the mapper's large `WMC_other` repeatedly. `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, and `membershipTenured` all share the same `Fiscal.startYear` definition, so the `-M<YY>` and `FY<YY>` segments stay consistent (verified in the audit line: registration `2026-09-01` \u2192 `M26` / `FY26`).",
